/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-2-//
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-3-// Minimal dict support. A dict value is `dictV(KS, VS)`: PARALLEL insertion-ordered key/value
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-4-// ValSeqs (Python dict order; keys distinct; re-inserting a key updates its value in place, keeping
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-5-// the original position). Concrete for krun (the ordered build + `.keys()` are the real ops); a proof
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-6-// over a SYMBOLIC dict passes `dictV(KS, WS)` with a symbolic key sequence KS and reads
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k:7:// `d.keys() = list(KS)`, then keeps each key opaque problem-locally.
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-8-//
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-9-// Only the pieces needed so far: a dict VALUE (so `{}` inside a mixed list evaluates and
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-10-// `isinstance(x, int)` rejects it), the `{k: v, ...}` literal, and `.keys()`. More dict ops (subscript
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-11-// / `.get()` / `.values()` / dict `==`) are added as dict problems need them — kept minimal + additive.
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-12-
--
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-15-  imports MPY-ITER
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-16-  imports MPY-METHODS
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-17-  imports MPY-LIST
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-18-
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-19-  // dict as PARALLEL ordered key/value ValSeqs (same length; keys distinct).
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k:20:  syntax Val ::= dictV(ValSeq, ValSeq)
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-21-
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-22-  // ==== DictExpr: {k: v, ...} literal. Eval each key then value, left to right, insert-with-dedup.
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k:23:  syntax KItem ::= #dictAcc(Entries, ValSeq, ValSeq)
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-24-                 | #dictKey(Expr, Entries, ValSeq, ValSeq)
